---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import shotHome from '../../assets/eventos/01-home.jpg'
import shotAgenda from '../../assets/eventos/02-agenda.jpg'
import shotMapa from '../../assets/eventos/03-mapa.jpg'
import shotEvento from '../../assets/eventos/04-evento.jpg'

const stack = [
  'React 18',
  'Vite',
  'React Router',
  'Tailwind CSS',
  'Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Storage)',
  'PostgREST',
  'Vercel serverless (Node)',
  'Leaflet + OpenStreetMap',
  'vite-plugin-pwa',
  'Vitest',
  'GitHub Actions',
]
---

<Base
  title="Case study — Eventos Região"
  description="How I designed and built Eventos Região: an inclusive, region-focused events platform on React + Supabase + Vercel."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <a href="/#projects" class="text-sm text-muted hover:text-text">← Back to projects</a>

    <header class="mt-6 border-b border-border pb-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-widest text-accent uppercase">Case study</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-text sm:text-4xl">Eventos Região</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        An inclusive platform to discover and promote local cultural, sporting and community events,
        organised by <strong class="text-text">city and proximity</strong> rather than by nationwide
        search. Built solo for a university extension project (UN SDGs 8 &amp; 11).
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm">
        <a href="https://eventos-regiao.vercel.app" class="font-medium text-accent hover:underline"
          >Live demo ↗</a
        >
        <a href="https://github.com/AndreiVDS/eventos-regiao" class="text-muted hover:text-text"
          >Source ↗</a
        >
      </div>
    </header>

    <Image
      src={shotHome}
      alt="Eventos Região home page"
      width={880}
      height={315}
      class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-border"
    />

    <article class="mt-10 space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">The problem</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          A book fair at the public library, a neighbourhood <em>festa junina</em>, a street race, a
          <em>boi de mamão</em> performance — these events are free, run by city departments,
          libraries and collectives, and have no ticket to sell. National ticketing platforms
          ignore them, so they stay invisible outside word of mouth. There was no single place to
          answer <em>"what is happening near me this weekend"</em> for a specific region.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">What I built</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          A full platform with three roles:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Visitors</strong> browse and filter events by city, category,
            date, price and format; a "near me" mode sorts by real distance to the venue and shows
            everything on a map.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Organizers</strong> create an account and submit events for
            free; they land in a moderation queue and the organizer tracks status, rejection reason
            and per-event stats.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">The team</strong> moderates the queue, manages cities from an
            embedded IBGE municipality list, reads contact messages, and watches a metrics panel
            (events by city, category, state and month).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          It ships as an installable <strong class="text-text">PWA</strong> and exposes a small
          public read API so other regional sites can embed the agenda.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <Image src={shotAgenda} alt="Event list with filters" width={430} height={310} class="rounded-xl border border-border" />
        <Image src={shotMapa} alt="Events on a map" width={430} height={310} class="rounded-xl border border-border" />
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Decisions &amp; trade-offs</h2>
        <dl class="mt-4 space-y-5">
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-text">One codebase, two runtime modes</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-muted">
              Without Supabase env vars the app runs in <em>demo mode</em> — data from local JSON,
              a fake session, writes to <code>localStorage</code> — so the whole thing (organizer and
              team flows included) runs with no backend. Made local development and review trivial.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-text">Security in the database, not just the app</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-muted">
              Row Level Security on every table: the public anon key is safe precisely because the
              policies constrain it. Anyone can insert an event, but only as <code>pending</code>;
              only the team can change status; the moderator allowlist is a table where each row is
              visible only to its own owner.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-text">"Near me" measures the venue, not the city</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-muted">
              The first version measured GPS → city centroid, which produced nonsense like
              <em>"5&nbsp;km from Jaraguá do Sul, from you"</em>. I added per-event coordinates
              (geocoded on submit) and a Haversine distance to the actual venue, with the city as
              fallback. A real correctness bug, caught by using it.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-text">Prerendered HTML for a SPA</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-muted">
              A post-build step renders static HTML per event and per city, plus
              <code>sitemap.xml</code>, so search engines and link unfurlers get real content and a
              proper preview card — not an empty React shell.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-text">Email that degrades quietly</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-muted">
              Transactional email runs from a serverless function as best-effort: no SMTP configured,
              or an organizer contact that is a phone number → nothing is sent and moderation works
              exactly the same.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-text">One source of truth for seed data</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-muted">
              A single script is the origin of the sample data; JSON, SQL seeds and placeholder art
              are all generated from it, so nothing drifts out of sync.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <Image src={shotEvento} alt="Event detail page" width={880} height={315} class="rounded-xl border border-border" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Where it landed</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <li>27 seed events across 16 cities and 9 states; live on Vercel as a PWA.</li>
          <li>68 unit tests over the pure logic (distance math, filters, metrics, RSVP), run in CI on every push.</li>
          <li>
            Accessibility built in: semantic structure, keyboard-operable menus, labelled inputs,
            charts backed by a data table, <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> honoured.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Stack</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
          {stack.map((t) => <li class="rounded border border-border px-2 py-1 text-xs text-muted">{t}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">What I'd do next</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Scheduled email ("your event is in 2 days", "new event in your city") with
          <code>pg_cron</code> and a subscriber list; a payment gateway for paid highlights
          (currently a manual Pix flow); and onboarding tools for a city tourism department to run
          its own official agenda.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-6 text-sm">
      <a href="/#projects" class="text-accent hover:underline">← Back to all projects</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
